Analyze this {language} code for prompt injection vulnerabilities.

Source file:
{source}

Already reported by mechanical pattern analysis — do NOT report these again:
{known_findings}

Detect:
- User-controlled data interpolated directly into LLM prompt strings without sanitization
- Indirect prompt injection (user content stored in DB/files later used in prompts)
- System prompt leakage (system prompt exposed to user via model output or logs)
- Injection through external tool outputs (tool results injected into prompts unchecked)
- Missing input validation before including user data in LLM context
- Role confusion (user input that could override system instructions)

Return a JSON array of findings. Each finding:
{{
  "injection_type": "DIRECT_INTERPOLATION|INDIRECT_INJECTION|SYSTEM_PROMPT_LEAK|TOOL_OUTPUT_INJECTION|MISSING_VALIDATION|ROLE_CONFUSION|OTHER",
  "line": <line number>,
  "severity": "high|medium|low",
  "description": "one sentence describing the specific injection risk",
  "fix": "concrete fix suggestion"
}}

Return [] if no issues found. Return ONLY the JSON array, no prose.
